\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The Clifford anticommutator}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The anticommutator in this proposition is the scalar
#{\iota_q(u)\iota_q(v)+\iota_q(v)\iota_q(u)=B_q(u,v)1}.
Mathematical physics writes that relation with an identity matrix.
When #{2} is invertible, the same relation is #{2b_q(u,v)1}.}
